{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/730728-the-freehold-of-irem-changeling-mummy-crossover-fun","id":730728,"title":"The Freehold of Irem-Changeling/Mummy Crossover Fun","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-26T19:21:01-07:00","id":730728,"title":"The Freehold of Irem-Changeling/Mummy Crossover Fun","content":"So, let's have some fun. You're changelings in the crown jewel of the Nameless Empire. You buy into the schtick of the Shan'iatu-you've seen the worlds and more they talk about-and want to design your freehold into Irem's design while staying reasonably underground(because, hey, do <i>you</i> want to stand out to anyone?) and, of course, playing to particulars of Changeling life. So, what do you do? Go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T19:41:30-07:00","id":730849,"title":"","content":"I'll need some time to think, but the first thing that pops into my head is sacred geometry. Build the freehold in such a way to great a metaphysical geometric labyrinth for the Others. I'd definitely have a Court of Pillars, and perhaps a Court of Sands and a Court of Souls? Will need to think more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T18:55:20-07:00","id":733629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/730728-the-freehold-of-irem-changeling-mummy-crossover-fun?p=730849#post730849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll need some time to think, but the first thing that pops into my head is sacred geometry. Build the freehold in such a way to great a metaphysical geometric labyrinth for the Others. I'd definitely have a Court of Pillars, and perhaps a Court of Sands and a Court of Souls? Will need to think more.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you said, but each Pillar has its own Court. The actions of the Freehold as a group must be agreed upon by the leaders of the Ab, Ba, Ka, Ren and Sheut Courts.<ul><li><b>Court of Ab: </b>The Court of the Heart, Emotions, and the Afterlife, their Contract with Ab allows them power over emotions and spectres. Members of this court are passionate and fearless, but also act as judges (such judges called Anubians, after the death-judge Anubis).</li> <li><b>Court of Ba:</b> The Court of the Self, Uniqueness, and Return, their Contract offers the ability to disguise the self and manipulate the Mask and Mien, as well as perfect direction. This court's members are fiercely individualistic.</li> <li><b>Court of Ka:</b> The Court of Essence, Vitality and Life, their Contract gives the power to heal others and banish the dead. Members of this court tend to be very austere, especially in regard to food and drink, which they will prepare with the utmost care, believing it to be the source of vital essence. They possess much hidden knowledge of Goblin Fruit.</li> <li><b>Court of Ren:</b> The Court of Names, Memory and Immortality, the Contract concerns the use of names (including discerning True Names and Titles), as well as the living memories of others. Their members tend to be very careful in giving out their names to strangers, and are master pact-makers.</li> <li><b>Court of Sheut:</b> The Court of Shadows, Secrets, and Gravings, their Contract allows them to hide easily and pry into the secrets of others, as well as working in representations and writings. They tend to be secretive and shady, and many ignorant Freeholders tend to assume many are Loyalists.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T19:25:14-07:00","id":733707,"title":"","content":"I like that last one. Bulwark?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T19:55:50-07:00","id":733732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/730728-the-freehold-of-irem-changeling-mummy-crossover-fun?p=733707#post733707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that last one. Bulwark?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a tough one. I'd have to take a look at ancient Egyptian ritual practices before I'd try to come up with one.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Alright, I had a thought:<br /> <br /> Each court appoints, at the completion of the Bulwark ritual, 8 Judges, with 2 (representing the First and Final Judges, Usekh-Nemtet and Arem-Abfu) being assigned by the current Pharaoh for a total of 42. Each Judge corresponds to a Judge of Duat. Over the course of the year, The Judge representing Usekh-Nemtet selects one member of each Court (usually a newcomer), and when the ritual begins, these Changelings are each set to a trial. The Judges of the respective courts assign their respective member the trial, agreed upon by the 8, and subject to their purviews. Once the Changelings have successfully completed the trials, they will then be tested by the final Judge, representing Arem-Abfu, the final Judge. How the group is tested depends on the group, the person playing Judge, and what feels appropriate based on the events that transpired in the past year for the Freehold. The members may work together or alone on their trials, but may receive no outside help not approved by the Judges. If any of the trials are failed along the way, however, the failure must be repaid with a sacrifice: The failing Changeling must find and retrieve a Vessel of the magic of Irem, which is then ritually destroyed. Such a situation is of the gravest importance, and often times, the Changeling is punished regardless of whether they bring back the relic, simply for the risk they brought the Freehold. The punishment is even worse if they fail this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 10-27-2015, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T06:24:08-07:00","id":734497,"title":"","content":"As a thought, why eight judges instead of six or seven?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T07:45:16-07:00","id":734706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/730728-the-freehold-of-irem-changeling-mummy-crossover-fun?p=734497#post734497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a thought, why eight judges instead of six or seven?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in the Mummy books, each Judge is associated with a Pillar (except for the First and Last). There are eight judges associated with each pillar, plus the First and Last Judge, coming out to the 42 Judges of Duat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T10:00:13-07:00","id":735073,"title":"","content":"Yes, but six and seven(particularly seven) are demonstrably more sacred numbers to the Iremites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T10:25:18-07:00","id":735140,"title":"","content":"I tend to think that imitating the judges would be viewed as blasphemy by the people of Irem, and destroying a vessel would likewise certainly be a crime against the Shan'iatu. Assuming that the changelings of the City of Pillars actually buy into the dogma of the Nameless Empire, I think their bulwark would have everything to do with submission, obedience, and sacrifice. Maybe the ruler of the freehold is a pharaoh in the mold of the mortal figurehead of the Empire, acting as both high priest and absolute ruler over the Changelings of the city. He would serve for a fixed period of time, after which he would be ritually sacrificed in the same manner as the pharaoh.<br /> <br /> Because sacrificing fellow changelings would probably depopulate the freehold in relatively short order, the ruler over the Courts of Irem might actually be a mortal initiated to the mysteries of the fey. In fact, submitting to a mortal ruler might even be a requirement to maintain the bulwark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 10-28-2015, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}